    {"step": 1, "tactic": "LSASS handle open via OpenProcess from non-EDR PowerShell", "technique": "T1550.002", "what_happened": "At 2026-05-17 12:48:14 UTC on WS-DEV-21, Sysmon EID 10 captured ProcessAccess on lsass.exe with SourceImage=C:\\Windows\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe, GrantedAccess=0x1000 (PROCESS_QUERY_LIMITED_INFORMATION). AMSI 4104 same time captured Add-Type DllImport kernel32 OpenProcess + Get-Process -Name lsass call. Rule 92050 triggered.", "chain_reason": "PowerShell P/Invoking OpenProcess on lsass.exe is the PtH precondition probe (verifying hash-extract feasibility). Legitimate apps that touch lsass are EDR/AV signed binaries — not powershell.exe."},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "net.exe use \\\\<target>\\IPC$ /user:<DOMAIN>\\<acct> <NTLM_HASH>", "technique": "T1550.002", "what_happened": "At 2026-05-17 12:48:40, Sysmon EID 1 captured net.exe with commandLine='net.exe use \\\\10.20.40.13\\IPC$ /user:CORP\\admin AABBCCDD00112233:FFEEDDCC99887766...' ParentImage=powershell.exe. Rule 92051 triggered.", "chain_reason": "net use against IPC$ with /user flag and a 32-hex-char string is the canonical PtH SMB pattern. Standard net use uses interactive password prompt — the inline 32-hex pseudo-password = NTLM hash injection."},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "DECISIVE — Security 4624 LogonType=3 NTLM on target WITHOUT preceding 4776 on DC", "technique": "T1550.002", "what_happened": "At 2026-05-17 12:48:42, SRV-FILES-03 Security EID 4624 LogonType=3, AuthenticationPackageName=NTLM, TargetUserName=admin, SourceNetworkAddress=10.20.40.21 (WS-DEV-21). However, DC-01 Security log shows ZERO EID 4776 (CredentialValidation) for account CORP\\admin between 12:48:30 and 12:48:42 — the credential was never validated by the DC. Rule 18101 triggered.", "chain_reason": "DECISIVE: 4624 LogonType=3 NTLM on a target server without ANY preceding 4776 on DC is the mathematical signature of Pass-the-Hash. Normal NTLM auth ALWAYS produces a 4776 on the validating DC; PtH bypasses DC validation by replaying the cached hash directly."},
